171
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,020
It's called the rule of three.

172
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:15,680
The rule of three.

173
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:15,920
Okay.

174
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:22,040
The rule states that if you have zero observed events in independent trials, the 95% upper

175
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:27,160
confidence bound for the probability of that event occurring is roughly three divided by

176
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:27,340
N.

177
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:27,740
Okay.

178
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:28,900
Let's plug the numbers in for that.

179
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:33,260
If our reference class is a single planet, Earth, our N is one.

180
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:33,540
Right.

181
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:34,180
One trial.

182
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:37,660
We have one trial, so we divide three by one, which gives us three.

183
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:42,160
But probability is expressed on a scale of zero to one.

184
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,700
You can't have a 300% chance of something happening.

